1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,085
This tutorial introduces four tools you
will use every day in

2
00:00:04,085 --> 00:00:08,170
Miftah: the home dashboard, global search,
notifications, and the Help Center.

3
00:00:08,170 --> 00:00:09,656
Begin on Home, Today.

4
00:00:09,656 --> 00:00:13,741
The Contract pipeline counts contracts by
stage: draft and to sign,

5
00:00:13,741 --> 00:00:17,826
upcoming, active, expiring within sixty
days, on notice, and settlement due.

6
00:00:17,826 --> 00:00:21,911
Below it, Needs you now lists the work
waiting for you:

7
00:00:21,911 --> 00:00:25,996
cheques to deposit, overdue payments,
contracts to post, and open tickets.

8
00:00:25,996 --> 00:00:28,596
Each row opens the records behind it.

9
00:00:28,596 --> 00:00:31,567
The cards underneath summarise
collections, pending dues, unit

10
00:00:31,567 --> 00:00:34,167
status, and overdue amounts for the
organisation.

11
00:00:34,167 --> 00:00:37,138
Treat these figures as signals, then open
the

12
00:00:37,138 --> 00:00:39,737
underlying list when you need the detail.

13
00:00:39,737 --> 00:00:41,223
Next, open global search.

14
00:00:41,223 --> 00:00:44,937
Select the search box in the header, or
press Command

15
00:00:44,937 --> 00:00:48,279
K on a Mac or Control K on Windows.

16
00:00:48,279 --> 00:00:52,364
Type part of a tenant name, unit,
contract, or cheque number.

17
00:00:52,364 --> 00:00:55,706
Typing Ahmed returns his tenancy contract
for unit A-101

18
00:00:55,706 --> 00:00:58,677
and each of his cheques, grouped by type.

19
00:00:58,677 --> 00:01:01,648
Results only include records your role can
open.

20
00:01:01,648 --> 00:01:02,763
Select the contract.

21
00:01:02,763 --> 00:01:05,734
Miftah opens the tenancy contract for unit
A-101

22
00:01:05,734 --> 00:01:08,333
directly, not a page of search results.

23
00:01:08,333 --> 00:01:10,933
Now open the bell in the header.

24
00:01:10,933 --> 00:01:14,275
The badge counts unread notifications, and
the preview lists

25
00:01:14,275 --> 00:01:17,618
the latest ones: a booking request and
meeting updates.

26
00:01:17,618 --> 00:01:19,103
Select View All Notifications.

27
00:01:19,103 --> 00:01:22,446
The full history can be filtered to
Unread, which

28
00:01:22,446 --> 00:01:25,788
shows only the items no one has
acknowledged yet.

29
00:01:25,788 --> 00:01:29,873
Review each item before you use Mark All
as Read; marking

30
00:01:29,873 --> 00:01:33,958
an item as read does not complete the work
it describes.

31
00:01:33,958 --> 00:01:38,415
Finally, open the Help Center with the
question mark in the header.

32
00:01:38,415 --> 00:01:41,014
Articles are grouped by topic and tagged

33
00:01:41,014 --> 00:01:43,243
with the roles they apply to.

34
00:01:43,243 --> 00:01:46,214
Search for roles, and open Roles and
Permissions.

35
00:01:46,214 --> 00:01:48,813
It explains what each role, from System

36
00:01:48,813 --> 00:01:51,413
Admin to Tenant, can see and do.

37
00:01:51,413 --> 00:01:54,755
Remember the pattern: the dashboard shows
what needs attention,

38
00:01:54,755 --> 00:01:58,098
search takes you to a record,
notifications tell you

39
00:01:58,098 --> 00:02:01,440
what changed, and Help explains how to do
it.
